From: TDVP Device Team <devices@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] pkg_hash: reject held candidates with unmet constraints

Keep held packages protected from replacement, but do not report an
incompatible held version as satisfying a dependency. The caller can try
another OR alternative or report an unsatisfied requirement. Selecting a
different version of this held package would bypass the hold protection.

--- a/libopkg/pkg_hash.c
+++ b/libopkg/pkg_hash.c
@@ -567,6 +567,13 @@
     abstract_pkg_vec_free(providers);
 
     if (held_pkg) {
+        if (constraint_fcn && !constraint_fcn(held_pkg, cdata)) {
+            opkg_msg(INFO,
+                     "Held package %s %s does not satisfy the requested constraint.\n",
+                     held_pkg->name, held_pkg->version);
+            return NULL;
+        }
+
         if (prefer_pkg) {
             opkg_msg(NOTICE,
                      "Ignoring preferred package %s %s due to held package %s %s.\n",
